---
import { STATS, STAT_KEYS } from "@bt/core";
import type { StatKey } from "@bt/core";
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { CORRECTIONS_EMAIL } from "../config";
import { DAILY_LEADERBOARD_PATH, DAILY_PATH, FRIENDLY_PATH } from "../lib/paths";
import { TIER_COLOUR, TIER_LABEL } from "../lib/tiers";

// One line per stat. Typed against StatKey, so adding a stat to @bt/core
// fails the typecheck until it's described here too.
const DEFINITIONS: Readonly<Record<StatKey, string>> = {
  club_goals: "Senior club goals in all competitions, for every club. Not asked about goalkeepers.",
  caps: "Senior international appearances. Nothing else counts as a cap.",
  apps: "Senior club appearances in all competitions, for every club.",
  ig: "Instagram followers, from a dated snapshot. The date is shown under the number.",
  fee: "The largest single reported transfer fee, shown with the year it was paid. Not adjusted for inflation.",
  igoals: "Senior international goals. Not asked about goalkeepers.",
  ct: "Club honours won, as listed on Wikipedia. Exactly what counts is set out below.",
  it: "Major international honours won with the national team.",
  clubs: "The number of senior clubs played for.",
  age: "Age today, worked out from date of birth. Only asked about living players.",
};

const stats = STAT_KEYS.map((key) => STATS[key]);
const reportHref = `mailto:${CORRECTIONS_EMAIL}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Correction")}`;
---

<Page
  title="How to Play and the Ten Stats Explained | Bigger Than Game"
  description="How to play Bigger Than Game, what each of the ten football stats means, what counts as a club trophy, where the figures come from and how to report a mistake."
  stickyBar
>
  <h1>
    About Bigger<em>Than</em>
  </h1>
  <div class="sublegend">Football Legends</div>

  <p>
    Bigger Than is a higher-or-lower game for football fans. Two retired players appear side by
    side, a wheel picks a stat, and you guess whether the hidden number is higher or lower than the
    one you can see. Get it right and the run goes on. Get it wrong and it's over.
  </p>
  <p>
    The difference is that <strong>the stat changes mid-run</strong>. You beat someone on caps, and
    then the question turns to Instagram followers, and the veteran loses to a winger with a boot
    deal.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-to-play">How to play</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Two players appear, with their names and nationalities. No stat yet.</li>
    <li>
      The wheel spins and lands on a stat. The plaque between the players shows which one, in the
      stat's colour.
    </li>
    <li>The first player's number is shown. The second player's is hidden.</li>
    <li>
      Pick <strong>Higher</strong> or <strong>Lower</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Right, and the player you just guessed becomes the one to beat, against someone new. Wrong,
      and the run ends. There's one life.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    A stat holds for a few rounds, then the wheel spins again. It only spins when the stat is
    changing, so watch the plaque before you pick. Two players never come up tied on the stat in
    play.
  </p>
  <p>
    The early rounds are gifts. As the run goes on the gaps between the two numbers narrow, until
    you need to actually know.
  </p>

  <h2>Friendly Mode</h2>
  <p>
    Friendly Mode is <strong>twenty questions with no timer</strong>. Take as long as you like over
    every answer, and get all twenty right to win the run. It's here so that anyone can play without
    a clock, and as a way to learn the game. It uses every player and every stat, and it has no
    leaderboard: your best score is kept on your device.
  </p>
  <p>
    You need a connection to play. The hidden number isn't sent to your browser until you've
    answered, so each answer is checked as you give it.
  </p>

  <h2>Daily Ranked</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={DAILY_PATH}>Daily Ranked</a> is <strong>one game a day, the same for everyone</strong>:
    twenty questions against the clock, fifteen seconds for the first and ten for each after it. A
    wrong answer or running out of time doesn't end it; you carry on to question twenty, and your
    score is how many you got right. Get all twenty and the bonus rounds begin, which go on until
    your first miss, each one adding a point.
  </p>
  <p>
    You choose the name you play under before you start, and you get one go a day. Every score goes
    on that day's <a href={DAILY_LEADERBOARD_PATH}>leaderboard</a>; when two players have the same
    score, the one who answered faster overall is placed higher. A new game starts at midnight UTC.
    If your page reloads mid-game, you can carry on where you were, but the clock keeps running.
  </p>

  <h2>The stats</h2>
  <p>
    There are ten. Each has a tier, and the plaque takes the tier's colour. The tier tells you how
    often a stat comes up, not what it's worth: every correct answer is one point.
  </p>
  <ul class="stats">
    {stats.map((stat) => (
      <li>
        <div class="stat">
          <strong>{stat.label}</strong>
          <span class="tier" style={`--tier: ${TIER_COLOUR[stat.tier]}`}>
            {TIER_LABEL[stat.tier]}
          </span>
        </div>
        <p>{DEFINITIONS[stat.key]}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2 id="club-trophies">What counts as a club trophy</h2>
  <span class="lab">Counts</span>
  <p>
    Every trophy listed under the club section of the Honours part of the player's English Wikipedia
    article, where the player's team won it. That includes one-match trophies such as the Community
    Shield, domestic super cups and the UEFA Super Cup, as well as leagues, cups, continental
    competitions and the Club World Cup.
  </p>
  <span class="lab">Doesn't count</span>
  <p>
    Runners-up and third places, individual awards, and youth, reserve or B-team honours.
    International honours don't count here either: they're the international trophies stat.
  </p>

  <h2 id="figures">Where the figures come from</h2>
  <p>
    Every figure is entered by hand from published sources and checked before it goes into the deck.
    Goals, caps and appearances are senior totals, in all competitions, for every club. Trophies
    follow the rules above. Instagram followers are counted on a stated date, which the card shows
    under the number, and ages are worked out from date of birth on the day you play.
  </p>
  <p>
    Figures aren't cited one by one on the cards. When someone reports a mistake, the figure is
    checked again against current sources and, if it's wrong, fixed in the next update.
  </p>

  <h3>Transfer fees</h3>
  <p>
    The fee is the largest ever paid for the player in a permanent move. Loans and youth moves don't
    count, and a player who never moved for a fee isn't asked about fees. Where a club published its
    figure, that's the one used, add-ons included; otherwise it's the most widely reported figure.
  </p>
  <p>
    So that every fee can be compared, each is converted to euros at the exchange rate for the year
    of the transfer: euro rates for modern fees, the European Currency Unit before the euro existed,
    and US dollars at one to one for the oldest deals. Fees are shown in millions of euros with the
    year of the transfer, and they're <strong>not adjusted for inflation</strong>, so an old record
    fee can look small next to an ordinary modern one. That's part of the game.
  </p>

  <h2>The players</h2>
  <p>
    Every player is retired, so caps, goals, trophies and fees don't change. Instagram followers do
    creep up, which is why they carry a date, and ages move on birthdays.
  </p>
  <p>
    Photos are freely licensed and credited on the <a href="/credits">credits page</a>. Players
    without a usable free photo are shown with their initial instead.
  </p>

  <h2 id="corrections">Spotted a wrong number?</h2>
  <p>
    At the end of a run, tap <strong>Something wrong with that card?</strong> The report carries the
    two players, the stat and both figures, so just say what's wrong and where you found the right
    one. Or email <a href={reportHref}>{CORRECTIONS_EMAIL}</a> with the player, the stat and your
    source. Corrections are checked and go into the next update.
  </p>

  <h2 id="suggest">Missing a legend?</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`${FRIENDLY_PATH}#suggest`}>Suggest a legend</a> for the deck. Retired players only.
    Anything else, like a bug or a typo? <a href={`${FRIENDLY_PATH}#problem`}>Report a problem</a>.
    None of the forms asks for your email or any other details.
  </p>
</Page>

<style>
  .stats {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
  }
  .stats li + li {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .stats p {
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .stat {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .stat strong {
    font-size: var(--fs-body);
  }
  /* A small plaque: the tier's colour, always with its name. */
  .tier {
    padding: 2px 9px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-pill);
    background: var(--tier);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: var(--fs-lab);
    font-variation-settings: var(--fv-caps);
  }
</style>
